From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:28:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: hi846: Run the Xperia 10 VI modules on their stock
 programs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Not for upstream as is.

Bind the front and ultra-wide Hi-846 modules of the Xperia 10 VI by
compatibles of their own, and run them on the stock camera stack's
sensor programs, loaded as firmware, at a 24 MHz clock. Power their
rails in the order each module's stock power table uses, read the
calibration in their OTP once and expose it through nvmem, and use the
full field of view of the ultra-wide module.

The board's device tree follows: the modules' compatibles, the front
module's rotation, and the link frequencies the programs run at.

The shape for upstream is the generic compatible with a firmware name,
and the generic fixes in this split out.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
